<body>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ HEADER -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="report-meta">Product Strategy · Competitive Intelligence · Q1 2026</div>
  <h1>Generative AI <span>Competitive Landscape</span><br>User Sentiment Analysis</h1>
  <p class="report-subtitle">A data-forward analysis of 41,729 app store reviews across ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Google Gemini, Perplexity, and Claude — examining satisfaction drivers, complaint themes, and sentiment-rating divergence.</p>
  <div class="report-stats-bar">
    <div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">41,729</span><span class="lbl">Total Reviews</span></div>
    <div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">5</span><span class="lbl">AI Applications</span></div>
    <div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">3.76</span><span class="lbl">Avg Star Rating</span></div>
    <div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">0.368</span><span class="lbl">Avg VADER Polarity</span></div>
    <div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">May 2025 – Mar 2026</span><span class="lbl">Review Period</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="content">

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ S1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW -->
<section class="section" id="executive-overview">
  <div class="section-label">Section 01</div>
  <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Three strategic takeaways derived from 41,729 user reviews. Read this section before diving into the detail.</p>

  <div class="takeaway-grid">
    <div class="takeaway t1">
      <div class="takeaway-num">Takeaway 01</div>
      <div class="takeaway-title">Microsoft Copilot Leads in User Satisfaction — by a Wide Margin</div>
      <div class="takeaway-body">Copilot scores 4.24 stars and a VADER polarity of 0.487, the highest of all five apps. It also has the lowest mismatch rate (8.05%) and the fewest complaint-flagged reviews (9.72%). Positioning against Copilot requires addressing the quality perception gap, not just feature parity.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway t2">
      <div class="takeaway-num">Takeaway 02</div>
      <div class="takeaway-title">Pricing Is the #1 Pain Point for Claude and Perplexity</div>
      <div class="takeaway-body">Claude leads all apps in Pricing/Subscription complaints (7.99% of reviews), followed closely by Perplexity (7.48%). These are the loudest signals of monetization friction. Meanwhile, Google Gemini and Microsoft Copilot attract far fewer pricing complaints (≤3.4%), suggesting their freemium tiers better match user expectations.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="takeaway t3">
      <div class="takeaway-num">Takeaway 03</div>
      <div class="takeaway-title">Perplexity and ChatGPT Face the Sharpest Accuracy Backlash</div>
      <div class="takeaway-body">Perplexity has the highest rate of Accuracy/Logic Issues (6.43%) and the lowest mean star rating among complaint-tagged accuracy reviews (2.04 stars). ChatGPT's accuracy complaints also carry strongly negative sentiment (VADER −0.176). Trust in factual correctness is a battleground where Claude and Copilot are comparatively better positioned.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Dataset Integrity Note</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6;">
      The source was documented as 50,000 reviews (10,000 per app), but the delivered CSV contains <strong style="color:var(--text)">41,729 rows</strong> — likely due to deduplication or filtering applied upstream. The dataset remains balanced enough for cross-app comparison (8,294–8,398 reviews per app, a &lt;1.3% spread). All KPIs are computed directly from this 41,729-row corpus. No values have been fabricated or extrapolated.
    </p>
    <div class="pill-row">
      <span class="app-badge badge-chatgpt">ChatGPT: 8,309</span>
      <span class="app-badge badge-claude">Claude: 8,339</span>
      <span class="app-badge badge-gemini">Google Gemini: 8,294</span>
      <span class="app-badge badge-copilot">Microsoft Copilot: 8,389</span>
      <span class="app-badge badge-perplexity">Perplexity: 8,398</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="section-hr">

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ S2: CROSS-APP SENTIMENT -->
<section class="section" id="app-sentiment-comparison">
  <div class="section-label">Section 02</div>
  <h2>Cross-App Sentiment Comparison</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Average star ratings, VADER sentiment polarity, and full rating distributions — two independent satisfaction signals compared side by side.</p>

  <!-- KPI cards -->
  <div class="card-grid card-grid-5" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">

    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-app"><span class="kpi-dot" style="background:var(--copilot)"></span>Microsoft Copilot</div>
      <div class="kpi-main" style="color:var(--copilot)">4.24</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">avg stars &nbsp;·&nbsp; polarity 0.487</div>
      <div class="kpi-bar-wrap">
        <div style="font-size:10px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:4px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1px;">Satisfaction</div>
        <div class="kpi-bar"><div class="kpi-bar-fill" style="width:84.8%; background:var(--copilot);"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kpi-card">
